# The Expo app is a separate project with its own dependencies and TypeScript
# config; it is not part of the Next.js build.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to the project root. Vercel's ignore matcher
# treats a bare "mobile" (or even "./mobile") as matching ANY path segment
# called mobile -- which silently dropped src/app/api/mobile/ and
# src/app/mobile/ from the deployment, breaking the native auth endpoints.
/mobile
.vercel
